        <register>
          <name>MISC_ARB_R_CTRL</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00001000</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>The register for CPU/HPERI to SRAM/PSRAM read arbitration</description>
          <resetValue>0x00F0F0F0</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>SHPERI_TO_SRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: LCDC
0x1: PPE
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[1]: slot 1 of arbiter
[2]: slot 2 of arbiter
[3]: slot 3 of arbiter
[4]: slot 4 of arbiter
[5]: slot 5 of arbiter
[6]: slot 6 of arbiter
[7]: slot 7 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[23:16]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CPU_TO_PSRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: CPU0
0x1: CPU1
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[1]: slot 1 of arbiter
[2]: slot 2 of arbiter
[3]: slot 3 of arbiter
[4]: slot 4 of arbiter
[5]: slot 5 of arbiter
[6]: slot 6 of arbiter
[7]: slot 7 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[15:8]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CPU_TO_SRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: CPU0
0x1: CPU1
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[1]: slot 1 of arbiter
[2]: slot 2 of arbiter
[3]: slot 3 of arbiter
[4]: slot 4 of arbiter
[5]: slot 5 of arbiter
[6]: slot 6 of arbiter
[7]: slot 7 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[7:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>SRAM_ARB_R_CTRL0</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00001004</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>The register for 32-bit HPERI master group to SRAM read arbitration</description>
          <resetValue>0x2D91A240</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>32B_HPERI_TO_SRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: GDMA
0x1: WIFI
0x2: USB/SDIO_BT/SDIO_WIFI
0x3: OTPC/SIC
0x4: SDIO_HOST
0x5: RMII
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[2:0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[5:3]: slot 1 of arbiter
[8:6]: slot 2 of arbiter
[11:9]: slot 3 of arbiter
[14:12]: slot 4 of arbiter
[17:15]: slot 5 of arbiter
[20:18]: slot 6 of arbiter
[23:21]: slot 7 of arbiter 
[26:24]: slot 8 of arbiter
[29:27]: slot 9 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[29:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>SRAM_ARB_R_CTRL1</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00001008</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>The register for 32-bit HPERI master group to SRAM read arbitration</description>
          <resetValue>0x2D91A240</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>32B_HPERI_TO_SRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>This is extended register of 32B_HPERI_TO_SRAM_ARB
[2:0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[5:3]: slot 1 of arbiter
[8:6]: slot 2 of arbiter
[11:9]: slot 3 of arbiter
[14:12]: slot 4 of arbiter
[17:15]: slot 5 of arbiter
[20:18]: slot 6 of arbiter
[23:21]: slot 7 of arbiter 
[26:24]: slot 8 of arbiter
[29:27]: slot 9 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[29:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>SRAM_ARB_R_CTRL2</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0000100C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>The register for CPU/LCDC/HPERI master group to SRAM read arbitration</description>
          <resetValue>0x0A50F0F0</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
